message: "If you use this formal research artifact, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "Lean LFM-to-Dirac Derivation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Partin"
    given-names: "G. D."
version: "0.17.0-research-dev"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gpartin/LeanDiracDerivation"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A noncanonical Lean 4 research derivation through DIRAC-017. It connects a
  positive two-field C19 action to a massive C19 Klein-Gordon tangent and
  proves that a cubical four-component Dirac Hamiltonian squares to its
  continuum symbol. It controls lattice/time corrections and derives the
  positive-frequency density/current limit from the same action. It also
  formalizes copy exchange under cube translation and a conditional cubical
  spin-one-half representation with exact conventional-spin intertwiners,
  explicit spectrum, continuous unitarity, 2pi sign reversal, 4pi return,
  and quarter-turn plus all-angle interpreted-Hamiltonian covariance.
  Dynamical selection and realization on a localized carrier, a physical
  electron, electromagnetic coupling, and uniqueness remain open. This
  development version is newer than the archived v0.15.0 release.
